p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1803,1405,77]},{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/81382f37b95747bdf87a/q-11-p-2-continuation.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,79,1405,97]}],"confidence":"medium","reviewNotes":["The source prints the ambient space as R^4 on page 1, but the displayed set notation on page 2 lists ordered triples (a,b,c), which is inconsistent in the source. Transcribed as printed."]},{"id":"81382f37b95747bdf87a-q-12","number":"4C","markdown":"Let $T:R^2\\to R^2$ be a linear transformation defined by\n\n$$\nT(x,y)=(x-y,2x+y).\n$$\n\nFind the $rank(T)$, $nullity(T)$ and hence verify rank-nullity theorem.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/81382f37b95747bdf87a/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,168,1405,200]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"81382f37b95747bdf87a-q-13","number":"5A","markdown":"Find the change of basis matrix $P$ from the basis\n\n$$\nB=\\{(1,1,1),(1,2,1),(0,0,1)\\}\n$$\n\nto the basis\n\n$$\nB'=\\{(1,1,0),(0,1,1),(1,0,1)\\}\n$$\n\nof $\\mathbb{R}^3$. Hence write down the change of basis matrix from $B'$ to $B$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/81382f37b95747bdf87a/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,360,1405,80]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"81382f37b95747bdf87a-q-14","number":"5B","markdown":"Find the cosine of the angle between the vectors $f=t^2+1$ and\n\n$$\ng=t\n$$\n\nin $P(t)$ (space of polynomials over real numbers) with the inner product\n\n$$\n\\langle f,g\\rangle=\\int_0^1 f(t)g(t)\\,dt.\n$$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/81382f37b95747bdf87a/q-14-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,432,1405,181]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"81382f37b95747bdf87a-q-15","number":"5C","markdown":"Let $u=(1,1,2,1)$. Find a basis and the dimension of the subspace $u^\\perp$. Also, find the projection of $u$ on the subspace spanned by set $\\{(1,1,1,-1),(1,-1,0,0)\\}$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/81382f37b95747bdf87a/q-15-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,605,1405,1275]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]}],"warnings":["Question 4B contains an apparent inconsistency in the printed source: the text says subspaces of R^4, but the displayed definitions use triples (a,b,c).","Transcribed from original page images with gpt-5.4. Automatic transcription is not independent human verification."]}
